## The ESG double bind

Badlands contributor [[erik-carlson|Erik Carlson]] gave woke capital its sharpest formulation in April 2023: get woke and go broke, don't get woke and go broke — you choose.{n} A company that adopts the agenda alienates the customers who actually buy its products; a company that refuses is excluded from [[esg|ESG]]-screened funds run by [[blackrock|BlackRock]], [[vanguard-group|Vanguard]] and [[state-street|State Street]], shrinking its shareholder base and depressing its valuation.{n}

Carlson argued that most CEOs would privately prefer prosperous, non-woke companies, but that some were installed precisely because they are motivated to promote the agenda — which is why, in his view, consumer boycotts are essential: without them, woke corporations can be both prosperous and woke and pay no price for pushing the agenda.{n} He read the cabal's willingness to sacrifice profit for narrative as a sign of desperation rather than strength.{n}
